course: dictionary
lesson: 12185
title: Words of sympathy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are gentle and respectful, and they help us know what to do and say. Condolence is one of them. When someone has died, people show they care by sending words of sympathy, and these words are called condolences. «The whole village sent their condolences to the family after the funeral.» The family has lost someone, so condolences must be kind messages that show sympathy.
explain: Look for clue words around the new word. «Everyone signed the book of condolence at the church.» A book of condolence is a book where people write kind messages for a family who is sad. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A message of sympathy fits. A party invitation or a game does not.
explain: Condolence can also mean the feeling of sympathy itself. «She felt deep condolence for her friend, so she sat with her all afternoon.» Here the feeling is shown by kindness. Words like «my condolences» are a polite way to say you are sorry for someone's loss.
fact: Condolences are words or messages of sympathy for someone whose loved one has died.
fact: «Condolence» can also mean the feeling of sympathy shown at a sad time.
fact: Condolences are usually plural: people offer condolences or send condolences.
fact: «My condolences» is a respectful way to say you are sorry about someone's loss.
fact: A «book of condolence» is a book where people write messages to a family after a death.
exercise: «The family received many cards of condolence after the funeral.» What are the cards of condolence? | *Cards with kind messages of sympathy | Cards with a map of the town | Cards with birthday jokes | Cards for winning a game
exercise: Mia whispered, «My condolences,» to her friend whose grandad had died. What did Mia say? | Happy birthday wishes | A promise to visit the park | A joke to make her friend laugh | *Words of sympathy for her friend's loss
exercise: «Everyone signed the book of condolence.» Find and copy one word from this sentence that means a message of sympathy. | *condolence | everyone | signed | book
test: «He offered his condolences to the family.» What does offered his condolences mean? | *Gave a kind message of sympathy about their loss | Asked them for money | Wrote a shopping list | Gave a loud speech about football
test: Why might people write in a book of condolence? | To borrow a library book | *To show sympathy for a family after a death | To play a quiz | To learn to draw
exam: Which phrase best matches the meaning of condolences? | A party invitation | *Messages of sympathy for someone who has died | A weather forecast | Instructions for a board game
